<title>USA: Glendale Fed acquires loan servicing rights.</title>
<headline>Glendale Fed acquires loan servicing rights.</headline>
<dateline>GLENDALE, Calif. 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Glendale Federal Bank on Tuesday said it will acquire servicing rights to a $12 billion, fixed rate mortgage loan portfolio of over 45,000 loans from Citicorp Mortgage Inc, a unit of Citicorp.</p>
<p>Citicorp Mortgage is acquiring the portfolio from Prudential Home Mortgage Co Inc, then selling it to Glendale Federal.  The deal will become effective May 30, Glendale Federal said in a statement.</p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>The loans are primarily jumbo California fixed-rate mortgage loans with an average age of two to three years.</p>
